ORDER: Plan a course of action to establish the bridgehead. #RiverCrossing #BlueForce


BEGIN ORDER:
As the Blue Force battalion commander, my immediate objective is to establish a bridgehead across the River at hex (10,6). The Red Force presence at both hex (10,6) and (11,6) needs to be neutralized or bypassed. Given the limited information and the need to concentrate force, I will initially mass the majority of our combat power at the river line to achieve surprise and force the Red Riverline to engage.

For COA A, I will move the Blue Support to (9,6) to create a diversion and draw the Red Riverline away from the primary objective at (10,6). Meanwhile, the Blue Bridgehead will hold its position to mask our true intentions while the Blue Screen provides security on our flanks.

For COA B, I will move the Blue Support to (9,6) and the Blue Screen to (8,6) to create a secondary front, aiming to pin down the Red Riverline and then attack it from the rear. The Blue Bridgehead will hold to mask our true intentions.

Considering the need for surprise and the concentration of force at the decisive point, COA A seems more aligned with the doctrine. It will create a diversion that forces the Red Riverline to engage, giving the Blue Bridgehead an opportunity to establish the bridgehead at (10,6).
